bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    unit_identifier_expression_statement_parse_error_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-26 webrender-checkable-margin-followup Linux aarch64 seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b interpreter: the TokenKind::Unit arm in parser_impl/core.rs (~l.821) routes only an assignment op, `.` or `[` to parse_expression_or_assignment; comparison/binary ops, `(` and newline go to parse_unit(), which expects a declaration name. Lane renamed the parameter to `suffix`. Pure-Simple parser (src/compiler/10.frontend) not checked: no full-CLI pure-Simple binary on this host."
    unit_identifier_expression_statement_parse_error_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: reproduced on fresh HEAD seed - fn f(unit: text) with statement unit == px fails parse: expected identifier, found Eq. Pure-Simple frontend has NO gap (unit is not a lexer token there; only newunit is; module routing gated on current_ident_is_unit_decl; fn-body parse_statement has no unit arm) - verified by driving compiler.core.parser + HirLowering on the seed interpreter, frontend spec test/01_unit/compiler/frontend/unit_identifier_expression_statement_spec.spl 4/4 PASS. Root cause (seed): src/compiler_rust/parser/src/parser_impl/core.rs:821 TokenKind::Unit statement arm used an allow-list routing to parse_expression_or_assignment; all other follow tokens fell into parse_unit whose expect_identifier fails. Patch prepared (inverted gate: parse_unit only when an identifier directly follows unit) but NOT built per lane constraints; seed-side executable spec test/01_unit/compiler/parser_unit_identifier_expression_statement_spec.spl added - currently fails to compile on the buggy seed with exactly the doc diagnostic (regression trigger), expect 3/3 after rebuild. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/frontend/unit_identifier_expression_statement_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/parser_unit_contextual_keyword_spec.spl"

bug_fix_strategies |bug_id, line_num, content|
    unit_identifier_expression_statement_parse_error_2026-11-26, 0, "A unit/newunit declaration is always `unit <Name> ...`: call parse_unit only when the next token is an Ident and send every other case to parse_expression_or_assignment (invert the allow-list). Add a parser spec for `unit == x`, `unit + 1`, `unit(…)` statements."

